  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Mercimek corbasi is the soup that sustains Turkey. It costs almost nothing to make, takes less than an hour, and produces a bowl of smooth, orange-hued soup that is much more than the sum of its parts."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The difference between a flat version and a great one lies in the final step: a small pan of butter is heated until foaming, Aleppo pepper is stirred in, and the whole thing is poured over each bowl just before serving. That hit of spiced butter is what lifts the soup from beige to memorable."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Red lentils need no soaking and cook quickly. The carrot gives natural sweetness; the cumin gives depth. Blend until completely smooth and pass through a sieve if you want a very silky texture, though it is not essential."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
